Hey [~accountid:6401d565314f508813822b2e] , here is the result of my investigation. 


*Technical explanation of the bug:*

The original problem here is not with the feature but with the map’s camera positioning logic in our codebase. The maps camera and its paddings consider only points (lat, lng) plotted on the map. i.e. the start point, the path, the pickup point, and the tool tip point. It doesn’t take the marker view’s height or width into consideration. i.e. Tool tip view size, pickup pin size, and start point tooltip view size. Hence in some devices, depending on the amount of map area visible, the marker views in the corners have a chance to get cropped. The bug is theoretically possible in iOS too. But their screen screen sizes don’t vary much so it is not easily evident. 

*Past situation:*

Initially, the bug was easily reproducible for Frankfurt Airport Terminal 2 (shown in the screenshot), because of the tooltip’s placement from BE response. 

*Current situation:*

Now, since it was not yet fixed in the client, the operations guys or BE changed the tooltip’s placement in such a manner that it is not towards the extreme corner of the screen. Hence it is not evident anymore. 

*Conclusion:*

Theoretically, the bug still exists, it is just not evident because the marker placements are adjusted by BE. But in the future, if we decide to implement some other feature or some other airport with the marker ending at the extreme corner, the issue can be visible again. My recommendation is to check out the linked [ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CLIENTAPP-18184] and see if it can be helpful. 

