*Removal of Inefficient Columns from L123 to Line 153:*

*_is_lastyear_* to *_in_previous_12_month_*.
[https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/a130940a6e254cce7bf1acdefb37749b536427f1/delivery/models/marts/eater/etl_delivery_order_order_items.sql#L124C3-L153|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/a130940a6e254cce7bf1acdefb37749b536427f1/delivery/models/marts/eater/etl_delivery_order_order_items.sql#L124C3-L153]

We need to *remove* certain time-based columns from our DBT incremental model. The columns in question use calculations relative to the current date ({{CURRENT_DATE()}}), namely:

{{is_lastyear}}
{{is_last16w}}
{{is_last4w}}
{{is_last1w}}
{{in_current_month}}
{{in_previous_month}}

etc.

The calculations in the provided SQL snippet are relative to the current date ({{CURRENT_DATE()}}). This means that the results for these columns are not static; they can change over time. For example, an order that is part of {{is_last1w}} today may not be part of {{is_last1w}} a week from now. Records that were processed and loaded into the data model in previous runs will have their time-based flags ({{is_last1w}}, {{is_last4w}}, etc.) frozen at the values they had at the time of processing. These flags will not update automatically, and as time progresses, they become incorrect. To keep these time-based flags updated, we would need to reprocess the entire data set or at least the affected rows frequently, which negates the efficiency gains that incremental processing is designed to provide.

Thank you!

